task.description:
We're a SaaS company with 50,000 support articles stored in Markdown files. Currently, our search is handled by this Elasticsearch query:

```
GET /support_articles/_search
{
  "query": {
    "multi_match": {
      "query": "{{user_input}}",
      "fields": ["title^3", "content", "tags^2"],
      "type": "best_fields",
      "fuzziness": "AUTO"
    }
  },
  "size": 10
}
```

The problem is users have to guess exact keywords. When someone searches 'how do I reset my password' they might not find the article titled 'Account Credential Recovery Process' even though it's the right answer. We want to move to semantic search so people can ask questions in plain English and find relevant articles based on meaning, not just keyword matching. Can you help us build a pipeline that indexes these 50,000 articles with embeddings and serves natural language queries?
